Z||000003||stimpy||01-28-2001||12:09 AM||||Alex, if you come to the next meeting of FCO, I'll show you up close how I put my enclosure together.  After turning y'alls 84 into a GT, a subbox will be easy money.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||01-28-2001||12:17 AM||||Ok, cool!  We'll most likely go to this time. Thanks!<P>Alex..||||reg||3
Z||000005||fropuff||01-28-2001||12:26 AM||||If you want to know how to build one, just ask me.  I bugged the crap out of stimpy when I did mine, and I feel as if I should help someone else a time or two.  Just say so if you want to know; anyone else too.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||01-28-2001||11:58 AM||||It's all good, fro. I was more then happy to help.  Besides, Alex lives right down the road from me, (well, about an hour and a half down) so if he wants to know how to build one, he needs to get his narrow backside on over to an FCO meeting so's I can check out his car!||||reg||1
Z||000007||G-Nasty||01-28-2001||11:36 PM||||You wont need that overhead thingy for an aftermarket subwoofer installation. That Performance Sound switch is for factory subwoofers. Get a namebrand amp and oxygen free wires that can run all your speakers and subwoofer. Kicker/Pro Punch and MTX rule.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bugsy||01-30-2001||01:49 PM||||doesn't putting it in the footwell make things a bit cramped for the passenger? I have a Kenwood 200 watts bridged into one 10" Sony Xplode sub, mounted behind the passenger seat. It gives a GREAT back massage...LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Thumper_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||01-30-2001||03:15 PM||||Of course it reduces the passenger foot room, but not too much to feel cramped.  The front of the box goes about to the passenger foot rest; the thing on the right hand side that has a vinyl-like material on it.  You can better understand if you look at stimpy's picture.  Mine's going to be an 8", not a 10" like his, so mine'll be a little more shallow, depth wise.  I was also thinking of getting a box like yours, kinda like fierosounds', but there's going to be no firewall cutting for me, thank you very much.  I think the best way is an 8" under the dash, then an 8 or a 10 in the floor, or a box in the front compartment, ported into the passenger compartment.  The firewall mount looks the nicest, but MAY not be safe.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||01-30-2001||06:10 PM||||Yes, having a big pre manufactured box dropped on the floor would definately eat up space.  A properly constructed enclosure will take up no more space then those pesky pedals do on the left side of the car. Checkitout...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high"> <BR>You can see that all of the enclosure is well behind the back of the console. From the front edge of the seat (fully back) to the speaker grill is 20".  There is no seat in the way to baffle all that sweet, crisp bass! I love it!||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||01-30-2001||08:04 PM||||also, having one behind the seat means you need to put the seat forward quite a bit, if not all the way. and of course this reduces passenger side room.<P>hey stimpy, when is that meeting? i don't know anything about the oklahoma club. i might want to get involved. thanks.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||3
